1
00:00:07,293 --> 00:00:11,751
Over the past months my articles have
taken up one question after another.

2
00:00:11,831 --> 00:00:13,653
Cause without causal power.

3
00:00:13,733 --> 00:00:15,908
Continuity without a carrier.

4
00:00:15,988 --> 00:00:18,340
How identities form in the meeting.

5
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,057
What a phenomenon is.

6
00:00:20,857 --> 00:00:25,034
Looking back over them, I see one
shape running through all of them.

7
00:00:25,866 --> 00:00:28,653
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

8
00:00:28,733 --> 00:00:32,924
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

9
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:35,524
There are two halves to the work.

10
00:00:35,604 --> 00:00:40,442
One half is negation: seeing that
nothing is found from its own side.

11
00:00:40,522 --> 00:00:46,461
The other half is formation: understanding
how a world without essence still appears.

12
00:00:46,541 --> 00:00:48,803
Vivid. Stable. Working.

13
00:00:49,621 --> 00:00:52,888
Start with negation, and
with what it has to face.

14
00:00:53,718 --> 00:00:58,489
One of the most important turns in
leaving a substantialist view is this.

15
00:00:58,569 --> 00:01:02,877
The things, the substrates,
and everything I took as given,

16
00:01:02,957 --> 00:01:08,706
undeniable and there from its own side,
turn out to be frameworks. I built them.

17
00:01:08,786 --> 00:01:11,713
And I grew so used to them
that I never questioned them.

18
00:01:12,538 --> 00:01:17,064
Substantialism is not mainly a
theory anyone chooses to believe.

19
00:01:17,144 --> 00:01:20,216
It is an innate, default
way of perceiving.

20
00:01:20,296 --> 00:01:23,491
It assumes that separate
nouns exist first,

21
00:01:23,571 --> 00:01:28,128
from their own side, and enter
into relations only afterwards.

22
00:01:28,945 --> 00:01:34,945
Ordinary grammar supports this every time
I speak. The wind blows. The person walks.

23
00:01:35,072 --> 00:01:39,381
Each sentence slips in a fixed
bearer, standing behind the action.

24
00:01:39,461 --> 00:01:44,911
Because the habit is so reliable, the act
of naming disappears into what is named.

25
00:01:44,991 --> 00:01:49,358
A convention feels like a fact
standing outside any framework.

26
00:01:50,165 --> 00:01:52,422
Direct experience is never like that.

27
00:01:52,502 --> 00:01:54,460
The flashing is the lightning.

28
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:56,185
The blowing is the wind.

29
00:01:56,265 --> 00:01:58,595
No seer stands behind the seeing.

30
00:01:59,409 --> 00:02:04,234
Nor is there a raw, unnamed given
lying underneath my concepts,

31
00:02:04,314 --> 00:02:09,274
waiting to be labelled. Vividness and
naming are mixed through and through.

32
00:02:09,354 --> 00:02:13,586
There is no seam between them, and
no unnamed floor at the bottom.

33
00:02:14,389 --> 00:02:17,447
Modern physics points
in a similar direction.

34
00:02:17,527 --> 00:02:22,216
Again and again, what was supposed to be
the bottom layer turns out to be defined

35
00:02:22,296 --> 00:02:27,234
by interaction and relation, rather
than by fixed properties of its own.

36
00:02:28,062 --> 00:02:32,470
But this view does not rest on
physics, and does not need it as proof.

37
00:02:32,587 --> 00:02:35,876
Physical theories are
themselves valid frameworks.

38
00:02:35,956 --> 00:02:39,685
Reliable within their
domains. Open to revision.

39
00:02:40,485 --> 00:02:44,073
More basically, a fixed
nature does not hold together.

40
00:02:44,153 --> 00:02:49,087
Anything proposed as standing on
its own undermines itself at once.

41
00:02:49,167 --> 00:02:53,421
To pick it out at all needs
contrast, context and naming:

42
00:02:53,501 --> 00:02:56,247
the very dependencies it claims to escape.

43
00:02:56,327 --> 00:03:01,505
And a thing with a fixed, independent
nature could never depend on conditions.

44
00:03:01,585 --> 00:03:04,635
It could never change.
It could never interact.

45
00:03:05,449 --> 00:03:08,928
Leaving this habit is not a
one-time change of opinion.

46
00:03:09,008 --> 00:03:13,548
The old picture comes back quietly
the moment attention is off duty.

47
00:03:13,628 --> 00:03:17,434
In my own experience, three
strands have to work together,

48
00:03:17,514 --> 00:03:20,835
again and again, each checking the others.

49
00:03:21,666 --> 00:03:25,164
The first strand: confirm
it in direct experience.

50
00:03:25,977 --> 00:03:29,579
Agreeing with dependency in
theory changes very little.

51
00:03:29,659 --> 00:03:35,358
It has to be seen directly, many times,
until it is no longer just an idea.

52
00:03:35,447 --> 00:03:41,447
For me this began with anatta, no-self:
looking for a seer behind the seeing,

53
00:03:41,547 --> 00:03:44,606
a hearer behind the
hearing, and finding none.

54
00:03:44,686 --> 00:03:49,760
Then it went on with ordinary
objects. A phone. A cup. A tree.

55
00:03:50,594 --> 00:03:52,838
But experience alone has a limit.

56
00:03:52,918 --> 00:03:55,800
Experience can become deeply non-dual.

57
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:59,454
A taste of clarity, of
presence with no centre.

58
00:03:59,534 --> 00:04:03,096
And yet the framework that reads
it can stay substantialist.

59
00:04:03,176 --> 00:04:08,055
Then the habit quietly turns a genuine
taste back into a hidden ground.

60
00:04:08,135 --> 00:04:11,601
Solid things are simply
replaced by a subtler substrate.

61
00:04:11,681 --> 00:04:13,408
A universal Awareness.

62
00:04:13,488 --> 00:04:15,383
A Presence with a capital P.

63
00:04:16,206 --> 00:04:19,378
The second strand: equip
the view with tools.

64
00:04:20,181 --> 00:04:25,033
Analytical tools bring thinking in line
with what experience has already shown.

65
00:04:25,113 --> 00:04:30,169
Some are simple and easy to carry,
like the chariot of the monk Nāgasena.

66
00:04:30,249 --> 00:04:32,995
Look for the chariot in
the wheels, the axle,

67
00:04:33,075 --> 00:04:35,658
the frame, and it is not found there.

68
00:04:35,738 --> 00:04:38,103
Not in the parts, not apart from them.

69
00:04:38,183 --> 00:04:43,959
Some tools are thorough and exacting,
like Candrakīrti's sevenfold analysis,

70
00:04:44,039 --> 00:04:46,803
and Nāgārjuna's Middle Way verses.

71
00:04:47,617 --> 00:04:50,621
The analysis has to
work as a pure negation.

72
00:04:50,701 --> 00:04:55,132
It removes a nature of its own,
and puts nothing in its place.

73
00:04:55,212 --> 00:04:59,765
Otherwise the habit simply moves
to a subtler level. A void.

74
00:04:59,845 --> 00:05:03,012
A dynamic process. A web of relations.

75
00:05:03,092 --> 00:05:07,174
Or a store of possibilities,
quietly standing underneath.

76
00:05:07,986 --> 00:05:11,321
The third strand: taste
the gradual loosening.

77
00:05:12,129 --> 00:05:16,451
Whatever is taken to exist from its own
side is gripped with the tightness that

78
00:05:16,531 --> 00:05:18,190
solidity invites.

79
00:05:18,270 --> 00:05:21,628
As view and experience
keep confirming each other,

80
00:05:21,708 --> 00:05:24,291
that grip loosens. Gradually.

81
00:05:24,371 --> 00:05:28,167
The emotional grasping, and the
subtler grasping of the mind.

82
00:05:28,981 --> 00:05:31,808
What is left is not a
special state to be guarded.

83
00:05:31,888 --> 00:05:34,322
Trying to keep it would
bring the fixing back.

84
00:05:34,402 --> 00:05:37,759
Instead, mind and matter
lose their felt weight.

85
00:05:37,839 --> 00:05:40,902
They become light, vivid, and workable.

86
00:05:41,705 --> 00:05:46,792
And here is the turn. Relentless
negation alone is only half the story.

87
00:05:47,626 --> 00:05:50,060
But there is a trap at exactly this point.

88
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:54,245
It decides whether the leap into
a substrateless view is made,

89
00:05:54,325 --> 00:05:55,689
or only circled.

90
00:05:56,510 --> 00:06:01,770
Having negated, the mind asks: if
these vivid appearances are not things,

91
00:06:01,850 --> 00:06:03,050
then what are they?

92
00:06:03,762 --> 00:06:06,631
That question is the
old view, still running.

93
00:06:06,711 --> 00:06:09,448
It has to be seen through, not answered.

94
00:06:10,257 --> 00:06:12,717
Step one. There is no substrate.

95
00:06:12,797 --> 00:06:18,166
No thing, no substance, no bearer
is found behind or beneath any

96
00:06:18,246 --> 00:06:21,372
appearance. Not out there. Not in here.

97
00:06:21,452 --> 00:06:25,399
Not as a ground of mind,
or energy, or awareness.

98
00:06:26,197 --> 00:06:30,234
Step two. So the question,
what is it, is invalid.

99
00:06:30,314 --> 00:06:33,576
It assumes something is there
with a nature of its own,

100
00:06:33,656 --> 00:06:35,899
waiting to be identified correctly.

101
00:06:35,979 --> 00:06:39,853
Take that something away, and the
question has nothing to land on.

102
00:06:39,933 --> 00:06:42,611
The answer is not hidden.
It is not nothing.

103
00:06:42,691 --> 00:06:44,432
It is not beyond words.

104
00:06:44,512 --> 00:06:46,339
The question was never valid.

105
00:06:47,153 --> 00:06:50,469
Step three. So the eight
extremes do not apply.

106
00:06:50,549 --> 00:06:52,426
All of them, all at once.

107
00:06:52,506 --> 00:06:54,586
Does it arise, or cease?

108
00:06:54,666 --> 00:06:58,296
Is it permanent, or annihilated?
Does it come, or go?

109
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:00,388
Is it the same, or different?

110
00:07:00,468 --> 00:07:04,070
Each asks what becomes of a
thing with a nature of its own.

111
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:08,581
They belong to the inherent view,
and make sense only inside it.

112
00:07:08,661 --> 00:07:11,081
They need not be refuted one by one.

113
00:07:11,161 --> 00:07:13,979
And the middle way is not a
middle answer between them.

114
00:07:14,781 --> 00:07:17,174
Step four. Watch the it slip in.

115
00:07:17,254 --> 00:07:21,236
Even the question, how does it
form, can carry the old view.

116
00:07:21,316 --> 00:07:24,347
The it is assumed before
any question is asked.

117
00:07:24,427 --> 00:07:27,758
It is never seen in the
appearing. It is supplied.

118
00:07:27,838 --> 00:07:31,222
A grammatical ghost,
that habit puts first:

119
00:07:31,302 --> 00:07:37,174
a subject waiting for its verbs.
It arises. It forms. It lasts.

120
00:07:37,254 --> 00:07:38,454
It ends.

121
00:07:38,990 --> 00:07:41,288
This is the same habit as the self.

122
00:07:41,368 --> 00:07:45,541
A knower, put behind the knowing,
now running through everything.

123
00:07:45,621 --> 00:07:48,109
Changing the question does not remove it.

124
00:07:48,189 --> 00:07:50,110
Only seeing the habit does.

125
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:55,028
Step five. The it is what
is formed, not what forms.

126
00:07:55,145 --> 00:07:57,497
Formation does not happen to a thing.

127
00:07:57,577 --> 00:08:01,274
The it is named in the forming,
together with its conditions,

128
00:08:01,354 --> 00:08:03,407
and is not found apart from them.

129
00:08:03,487 --> 00:08:07,252
The cup formed on the potter's
wheel is valid, and it works.

130
00:08:07,332 --> 00:08:11,152
Heard as a bearer that was there first
and then went through the forming,

131
00:08:11,232 --> 00:08:13,819
it is as invalid as, what is it.

132
00:08:14,625 --> 00:08:19,232
Try it. Hold anything. A
cup. A sound. A thought.

133
00:08:19,312 --> 00:08:22,425
Notice the pull to ask,
what is this, really.

134
00:08:22,505 --> 00:08:25,523
See that the pull already
assumes a thing in there.

135
00:08:25,603 --> 00:08:27,452
Drop the it, not the cup.

136
00:08:27,532 --> 00:08:32,362
The cup is still fully here, vivid and
working. And I still call it the cup.

137
00:08:33,194 --> 00:08:35,587
That is the other half: formation.

138
00:08:35,667 --> 00:08:38,997
How a world empty of
essence still appears vivid,

139
00:08:39,077 --> 00:08:40,958
stable and workable.

140
00:08:41,777 --> 00:08:46,506
In this view, a phenomenon is a vivid
appearing that is not found when looked

141
00:08:46,586 --> 00:08:49,604
for, even while it appears so vividly.

142
00:08:49,684 --> 00:08:53,182
Every appearance has three
features, at the same time.

143
00:08:53,997 --> 00:08:57,952
It is vivid and clear. Nothing
is dimmed or taken away.

144
00:08:58,032 --> 00:09:01,172
Its clarity belongs to
the appearing itself.

145
00:09:01,252 --> 00:09:03,020
A sound is clear as sound.

146
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:05,058
A colour is vivid as colour.

147
00:09:05,138 --> 00:09:08,228
No witness behind it is
needed to light it up.

148
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:15,049
It is not found. Searched for, it
has no core, no edge, no location.

149
00:09:15,176 --> 00:09:19,009
Not out there in the world.
Not in here, in a private mind.

150
00:09:19,089 --> 00:09:22,995
And not even nowhere, since
nowhere is just one more place.

151
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:27,374
And it is dependently arisen,
and validly functioning.

152
00:09:27,454 --> 00:09:31,509
It shows up only when its conditions
meet. And it works completely.

153
00:09:32,326 --> 00:09:35,779
This third point is the one I
have had to come back to most.

154
00:09:35,859 --> 00:09:37,831
At first it sounds so strange.

155
00:09:37,911 --> 00:09:40,792
Habit equates being there
with being independent.

156
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:44,610
It hears naming as a thin
sticker on a thing already there.

157
00:09:44,690 --> 00:09:48,320
It pictures causes as one
substance pushing another.

158
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:51,082
So empty sounds flimsy. Ghostly.

159
00:09:51,914 --> 00:09:53,818
But empty does not mean weak.

160
00:09:53,898 --> 00:09:57,962
A car with no essence can still
injure you. Medicine still heals.

161
00:09:58,042 --> 00:09:59,882
A cup still holds hot tea.

162
00:10:00,689 --> 00:10:03,353
Take an apple, tossed from hand to hand.

163
00:10:03,433 --> 00:10:07,266
At once, habit supplies
the impression of a hard,

164
00:10:07,346 --> 00:10:09,608
heavy thing standing on its own.

165
00:10:10,413 --> 00:10:14,558
Yet when I look closely, the apple is
not found apart from the streams of

166
00:10:14,638 --> 00:10:17,796
consciousness. And it is
not made by them either.

167
00:10:18,614 --> 00:10:23,942
Hardness, coolness and weight arise
only as touch meets skin and fruit.

168
00:10:24,022 --> 00:10:28,167
The red shifts to orange under
candlelight, and to grey at dusk.

169
00:10:28,247 --> 00:10:31,297
It arises with light, eye and attention.

170
00:10:32,117 --> 00:10:35,855
When the habitual knot is
untied, nothing is missing.

171
00:10:35,935 --> 00:10:40,379
The apple can still be tossed.
Still eaten. It still nourishes me.

172
00:10:40,459 --> 00:10:45,433
Its solidity and its effects arise
because this vivid pattern meets hands,

173
00:10:45,513 --> 00:10:48,196
gravity and bodies, reliably.

174
00:10:49,017 --> 00:10:51,015
One guardrail stays in place.

175
00:10:51,095 --> 00:10:55,132
Consciousness is not a new floor
in here, producing the apple.

176
00:10:55,212 --> 00:10:58,869
Mind and matter are two cuts
in the same vivid appearing.

177
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:03,262
Neither is the substrate underneath
the other. Both are named together.

178
00:11:04,082 --> 00:11:08,490
The same two halves run through the
rest of my recent work. Briefly, then.

179
00:11:09,359 --> 00:11:14,225
First, cause. Strike a match, and
slow the film down as far as you like.

180
00:11:14,305 --> 00:11:16,806
At every frame, something is happening.

181
00:11:16,886 --> 00:11:20,991
At no frame does a finished
flame cross over from nowhere.

182
00:11:21,071 --> 00:11:24,963
And still, she lit the fire
at eight is perfectly valid.

183
00:11:25,773 --> 00:11:28,709
Causes work. Rice grows from rice seed.

184
00:11:28,789 --> 00:11:30,992
Bread without yeast stays flat.

185
00:11:31,072 --> 00:11:36,032
What is never found is a causal power: a
force sitting inside the cause from its

186
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:39,773
own side, handed across
a gap to the effect.

187
00:11:40,598 --> 00:11:43,181
So I keep three senses of cause apart.

188
00:11:43,261 --> 00:11:46,252
A producer with its own power: refused.

189
00:11:46,332 --> 00:11:48,752
Conditions coming together: kept.

190
00:11:48,832 --> 00:11:52,801
A link that attention singles
out and names: kept too.

191
00:11:52,881 --> 00:11:55,736
Conditions are not a
basement under the appearing.

192
00:11:55,816 --> 00:11:59,689
Conditions are the appearing,
cut into parts for explaining,

193
00:11:59,769 --> 00:12:01,379
and for getting things done.

194
00:12:02,189 --> 00:12:07,734
When no gap and no producer are found, the
question of why anything appears at all is

195
00:12:07,814 --> 00:12:13,046
retired. What remains is called
spontaneous presence. Not uncaused.

196
00:12:13,126 --> 00:12:14,500
Not a hidden source.

197
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:19,124
Just dependent arising itself,
met without the habit of fixing.

198
00:12:19,942 --> 00:12:21,724
Second, continuity.

199
00:12:21,804 --> 00:12:26,398
If nothing persists from its own side,
what carries me from this moment to the

200
00:12:26,478 --> 00:12:27,678
next?

201
00:12:28,274 --> 00:12:31,686
The question rests on a gap
that thought drew first.

202
00:12:31,766 --> 00:12:34,200
In the living moment it never comes up.

203
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,993
Each moment is complete.

204
00:12:36,073 --> 00:12:38,344
And a carrier would never solve it anyway.

205
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:41,020
Whatever links one moment to the carrier,

206
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:45,767
and the carrier to the next, needs
bridges of its own. Without end.

207
00:12:46,577 --> 00:12:51,673
As Nāgārjuna says, whatever arises in
dependence on something is neither that

208
00:12:51,753 --> 00:12:54,554
very thing, nor wholly other than it.

209
00:12:54,634 --> 00:12:59,567
Like a lamp burning through the night,
continuity is named across moments that

210
00:12:59,647 --> 00:13:02,081
condition one another reliably.

211
00:13:02,161 --> 00:13:04,558
Nothing travels from one to the next.

212
00:13:05,373 --> 00:13:10,700
Nothing is lost. Memory, learning,
responsibility and karma hold.

213
00:13:10,780 --> 00:13:15,216
And nothing is fixed. Habits can
loosen. Character can change.

214
00:13:16,087 --> 00:13:18,276
Third, the words themselves.

215
00:13:18,356 --> 00:13:22,298
Both views use the same words,
so the words have to be sorted.

216
00:13:22,378 --> 00:13:28,045
Heard by the logic of substance, dependent
arising means things that already exist,

217
00:13:28,125 --> 00:13:30,015
linked in a vast web.

218
00:13:30,095 --> 00:13:35,654
Meant by the logic of dependency, it means
things identified only in dependence.

219
00:13:35,734 --> 00:13:40,305
Relation and what is related are
named together. Neither comes first.

220
00:13:41,117 --> 00:13:45,031
Emptiness, heard the first
way, is a blank void,

221
00:13:45,111 --> 00:13:47,721
or a hidden reservoir behind things.

222
00:13:47,801 --> 00:13:53,292
Meant the second way, it is simply
this: no nature of its own is found,

223
00:13:53,372 --> 00:13:56,010
in appearances that are vivid and working.

224
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:58,211
And the word real is retired.

225
00:13:58,291 --> 00:13:59,977
Working, conventionally.

226
00:14:00,057 --> 00:14:02,807
Not found from its own side, ultimately.

227
00:14:03,609 --> 00:14:07,877
If things existed with fixed
natures, nothing could ever meet.

228
00:14:07,957 --> 00:14:10,662
Two things with sealed
edges could never touch.

229
00:14:10,742 --> 00:14:13,805
And if they merged, they
would collapse into one.

230
00:14:14,605 --> 00:14:17,772
In dependent arising,
meeting means something else.

231
00:14:17,852 --> 00:14:22,446
The two sides define each other
in one stroke. A hand touches ice.

232
00:14:22,526 --> 00:14:26,114
They meet, with no gap
crossed, and no fusion.

233
00:14:26,194 --> 00:14:28,728
And the meeting itself
is not a third thing.

234
00:14:29,537 --> 00:14:34,864
Looking back over all these articles,
they say one thing, again and again.

235
00:14:34,944 --> 00:14:36,309
The it is never needed.

236
00:14:37,125 --> 00:14:40,604
Not in experience. The
flashing is the lightning.

237
00:14:40,684 --> 00:14:42,688
No lightning stands behind it.

238
00:14:43,489 --> 00:14:48,359
Not in formation. The it is formed,
named together with its conditions.

239
00:14:49,181 --> 00:14:50,351
Not in causes.

240
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:55,396
Conditions work without causal power,
and no it carries the power across.

241
00:14:56,193 --> 00:15:00,338
Not in functioning. The cup holds
tea, and the car can injure.

242
00:15:00,418 --> 00:15:02,163
Neither needs a core to do it.

243
00:15:02,965 --> 00:15:08,161
Not in continuity. Rice seed yields
rice, and nothing is carried across.

244
00:15:08,969 --> 00:15:12,942
Not in the meeting. No glue holds
self-standing things together.

245
00:15:13,749 --> 00:15:17,025
And so there is no it to
undergo the eight extremes.

246
00:15:17,105 --> 00:15:19,674
With none there, they
are not false answers.

247
00:15:19,754 --> 00:15:21,567
They are invalid questions.

248
00:15:22,369 --> 00:15:26,609
Many teachers, rightly, say the
eight extremes do not apply.

249
00:15:26,689 --> 00:15:31,487
It is Nāgārjuna's own opening verse,
and the traditions that say it point at

250
00:15:31,567 --> 00:15:35,196
something real. But it is
often said with a large gap.

251
00:15:35,276 --> 00:15:39,598
It is not shown why they do not apply:
that the it they need was never there.

252
00:15:39,678 --> 00:15:42,646
Nor is it shown how the
world still works without it.

253
00:15:43,482 --> 00:15:45,658
Then the gap is crossed by a leap.

254
00:15:45,738 --> 00:15:50,114
After freedom from all elaborations
comes spontaneous presence,

255
00:15:50,194 --> 00:15:53,307
presented as the end of all speech.

256
00:15:53,387 --> 00:15:55,608
Silence, as the final answer.

257
00:15:56,422 --> 00:16:00,663
I do not take that route. Silence
keeps the it, only out of reach.

258
00:16:00,743 --> 00:16:04,929
The habit only rests, and slips
back into the next sentence.

259
00:16:05,009 --> 00:16:11,009
And conventions are left unexplained,
so presence is easily heard as a ground:

260
00:16:11,096 --> 00:16:13,847
the final it, behind appearances.

261
00:16:14,653 --> 00:16:17,834
Dzogchen at its best
does not stop at silence.

262
00:16:17,914 --> 00:16:23,914
Read with Mipham, spontaneous presence
is dependent arising met without fixing,

263
00:16:24,109 --> 00:16:26,135
and the two truths stay one.

264
00:16:26,215 --> 00:16:30,297
Where I part is from a presentation
of the leap as the end of speech.

265
00:16:31,110 --> 00:16:34,264
Speech was never the problem.
The it heard in it was.

266
00:16:34,344 --> 00:16:38,544
Once the it is seen through, words
and names do not have to stop.

267
00:16:38,624 --> 00:16:41,098
They are used freely, and they work.

268
00:16:41,178 --> 00:16:44,549
The conventional is not a
lower floor to leave behind.

269
00:16:44,629 --> 00:16:48,897
The ultimate is not a silence to
leap into. They are one appearing.

270
00:16:48,977 --> 00:16:50,912
Named, and not found.

271
00:16:51,730 --> 00:16:53,226
The Buddha said it plainly.

272
00:16:53,306 --> 00:16:57,887
Milk becomes curds, curds become
butter, butter becomes ghee.

273
00:16:57,967 --> 00:17:00,713
While it is milk, it is not called curds.

274
00:17:00,793 --> 00:17:04,585
Nothing is carried, yet each
name is right in its time.

275
00:17:04,665 --> 00:17:07,832
These are the world's
common usages, he says,

276
00:17:07,912 --> 00:17:10,794
which the Realized One
uses to communicate,

277
00:17:10,874 --> 00:17:12,674
without getting stuck on them.

278
00:17:13,489 --> 00:17:16,765
Even the first it, the
I, is used this way.

279
00:17:16,845 --> 00:17:19,985
One who is fully freed
still says, I speak.

280
00:17:20,065 --> 00:17:22,797
Skillful, understanding
the world's labels,

281
00:17:22,877 --> 00:17:25,859
they use these terms as mere expressions.

282
00:17:26,682 --> 00:17:29,673
Tsongkhapa makes the same point as method.

283
00:17:29,753 --> 00:17:33,138
As long as appearance and
emptiness seem separate,

284
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:36,276
the Buddha's meaning is not yet realized.

285
00:17:36,356 --> 00:17:41,792
The view is complete when merely seeing
dependent arising undoes the grasping.

286
00:17:41,872 --> 00:17:43,319
No leap beyond it.

287
00:17:44,121 --> 00:17:48,402
And the one who sees it most
clearly, for me, is Dōgen.

288
00:17:48,482 --> 00:17:53,348
The old saying runs: a painted
rice cake does not satisfy hunger.

289
00:17:53,428 --> 00:17:55,060
Dōgen turns it over.

290
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:59,489
There is no remedy for satisfying
hunger other than painted rice cakes.

291
00:17:59,569 --> 00:18:03,298
Without painted hunger, you
never become a true person.

292
00:18:04,130 --> 00:18:06,958
There is no unpainted
cake behind the painting.

293
00:18:07,038 --> 00:18:08,697
No it behind the convention.

294
00:18:08,777 --> 00:18:13,348
The painting is not a poor copy,
waiting to be dropped. It feeds.

295
00:18:14,153 --> 00:18:17,392
So, with both halves in
place, what has changed?

296
00:18:18,226 --> 00:18:20,510
Nothing has been taken
away from the world.

297
00:18:20,590 --> 00:18:22,634
And no new ground has been added.

298
00:18:23,449 --> 00:18:26,847
The apple is still red.
The car is still dangerous.

299
00:18:26,927 --> 00:18:28,736
The cup still holds hot tea.

300
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,846
A friend's voice is still warm.

301
00:18:31,661 --> 00:18:34,425
What has gone is only the
floor that was never there.

302
00:18:35,241 --> 00:18:38,109
What remains is not a
final picture to defend,

303
00:18:38,189 --> 00:18:40,446
but the freedom of not needing one.

304
00:18:40,526 --> 00:18:45,052
Each appearance is met as it
is. Vivid. Exact. Workable.

305
00:18:45,132 --> 00:18:47,624
Releasing itself as it arises.

306
00:18:48,445 --> 00:18:52,812
Light and complete, with nothing
to hold, and no one holding.

